## Summary

I built the native Apple (SwiftUI) **`AnalyticsSummaryWidget`** at parity with `features/dashboard/widgets/AnalyticsSummaryWidget.tsx`, following the established `WeeklySummaryCardWidget` decomposition. **9 files** in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/`:

- **Models / Adapter** — pure, SI→display projection ported *verbatim* from the web (distance `÷1609.344`, the widget-local `×1.60934` efficiency factor, `costPerDist`, `hasData`, `fmtNumber`/`formatCurrency`).
- **Model** — P1/S8 state-holder seam (`AnalyticsSummarySource`, no HTTP in the view), P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, canonical registry (`analytics-summary`, 2×2 / 1×2 / 4×40), P1/S10 i18n facade with the interpolated `Cost / {{unit}}` label.
- **Tile / Content / Widget** — compact count-up hero (web `AnimatedNumber`), responsive 2-/4-col `StatCard` grid, **Swift Charts** sparkline row (web `Sparkline`), every state (loading/empty/error/stale/offline/content), VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type, reduce-motion.
- **Previews / Tests / .strings** — per-state previews, **28 unit tests** (adapter parity, phases, model, registry, a11y), full i18n catalog.

**Verification — green on both platforms (real xcodebuild, after building the KMP `Shared.xcframework`):**
- iOS full app build ✅ + my 28 tests ✅; macOS full app/test-bundle build ✅ + my 28 tests ✅
- swiftformat (whole tree) ✅ · swiftlint (my files) ✅ · placeholder check (gate-exact) ✅ · Swift 6 strict-concurrency typecheck (iOS+macOS) ✅

**`STATUS=BLOCKED` (honest).** The aggregate gate cannot reach `EXIT=0` within my allowed-files scope due to **three external causes**, all documented with proof in the log:
1. A **pre-existing swiftlint violation in a sibling file** (`LiveSignalSparklinesWidget.Builder.swift:158`, baseline commit `1ce15b48b`) — outside my allowed files, so unfixable here; it fails the lint step even on ideal CI.
2. **macOS code-signing** — entitlements need a dev certificate absent in this headless runner (compilation itself succeeds unsigned).
3. **Flaky full-suite under ~15-way runner contention** (load 130–305) — the test host crashed/relaunched, *skipping* my suites; all 3 named failing tests **pass in isolation**.

Per the binding **"No commit on red"** covenant, I did **not** commit — the complete, verified surface sits in the working tree (`git status` shows the 9 untracked files + the log). It's ready to commit once the sibling lint violation is fixed by its owner and a signed/uncontended runner is used.

